From 8adcf35d1108a7ed22dc52b41b07eb30daed8df7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:54:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] surface: zoom the picture of a surface, with no change to the
 grid

A pinch in Macterm zooms the picture of a pane, as a pinch zooms a page
in a browser. The font size, the grid and the pty size must not change,
so the zoom is a view transform: scale about an anchor point, then a
pan. Every other position stays in base surface pixels, and the zoom
applies last.

renderer.Zoom holds the transform and its math. resolve clamps the
scale to 1 through 3, the anchor to the surface, and the pan so that
the zoomed picture covers the surface. A value that is not finite is no
zoom. The render state keeps the request (renderer.State.zoom), and the
surface resolves it against its size at each use, so a resize needs no
update.

The surface applies the inverse where a pointer becomes a cell
(posToViewport, posToPin, mouse reports, the x of a selection) and the
forward in imePointScaled, so each popover that anchors to the cursor
follows the zoom. ghostty_surface_set_zoom sets the request, in points.

The renderer does not draw the zoom yet.
